        "image": "shopify://shop_images/601a5177-28a7-493f-8def-0eacb288616d.png",
        "layout": "image_first",
        "eyebrow": "What It's For",
        "heading": "Made For KP And Strawberry Skin",
        "heading_size": "h1",
        "text": "<p>Those small rough bumps on the backs of your arms and thighs are <strong>keratosis pilaris</strong> — KP for short. On your legs it shows up as the dotted look people call strawberry skin, most obvious right after you shave. It's extremely common, it's harmless, and it's stubborn: ordinary body lotion sits on top of it and changes nothing.</p><p>This resurfacing cream works on the texture itself. It smooths and softens the surface while a hydrating base keeps skin nourished, so you're not trading comfort for smoothness the way harsh scrubs make you.</p>",
        "button_label": "",
        "button_link": "",
        "button_style_secondary": true,
        "section_color_scheme": "scheme-2",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-2",
        "padding_top": 48,
        "padding_bottom": 48
      }
    },
