    "straw_faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_what": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What are KP and “strawberry skin”?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p><strong>Keratosis pilaris (KP)</strong> is the small, rough bumps that appear most often on the backs of the arms and the thighs — sometimes called chicken skin. <strong>Strawberry skin</strong> is the related dotted look on the legs, most visible after shaving. Both are very common and completely harmless. This cream is made to smooth how they look and feel; it isn't a medical treatment, so see a dermatologist if your skin is painful, inflamed or not settling.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_where": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where on my body can I use it?",
            "icon": "silhouette",
            "row_content": "<p>Anywhere the texture bothers you — the backs of the upper arms and the thighs are the classic KP spots, and legs are where strawberry skin shows most. It's formulated for body skin, so keep it off your face and away from broken skin.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_when": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long until I see a difference?",
            "icon": "stopwatch",
            "row_content": "<p>Skin texture changes slowly. Most body-resurfacing routines need consistent daily use before the difference is obvious, so give it a full month of regular use before you decide. Skipping days is what stalls progress.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_shaving": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I use it after shaving or waxing?",
            "icon": "washing",
            "row_content": "<p>Wait until the day after. Freshly shaved or waxed skin is more reactive, and giving it 24 hours keeps things comfortable. Day-to-day, applying after your shower is the easiest way to remember it.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_greasy": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will it feel greasy under clothes?",
            "icon": "bottle",
            "row_content": "<p>Massage it in fully and give it a minute to settle before you dress. If you're applying at night, it has all the time it needs to sink in while you sleep.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_sensitive": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is it suitable for sensitive skin?",
            "icon": "heart",
            "row_content": "<p>Patch test first, as you would with any new product: apply a small amount to your inner arm and leave it 24 hours. Check the full ingredient list on the carton if you have known sensitivities, and stop use if you get irritation.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_what",
